# Verify before PRs

Before opening a new pull request, or updating an existing PR with code changes:

1. Run the **test-guardian** subagent. Do not skip because tests "probably pass." Do not substitute a full Playwright matrix. TestGuardian picks Jest, API4, and/or `make test-server` from the diff (and a single Chrome Playwright spec only when the skill says the change is user-visible UI).
2. If TestGuardian reports failures, fix them or say what you did not run and why before creating the PR.

## Visual verification (when applicable)

Run this **in addition to** TestGuardian when the diff changes what a user sees or clicks: `webapp/channels` components, CSS, layout, routing, client state, or rendered copy.

Skip visual verification for Go-only, API-only, config, docs, or test-only diffs. Say that you skipped it and why.

When it applies:

- Exercise the changed flow in the running app the way a user would (click, type, submit, navigate). Local UI is `http://localhost:8065`. A single screenshot is not verification.
- Check other pages or routes that share the state, data, or components you touched.
- Check empty, error, and flag/route variants the change actually hits — not only the happy path.
- If layout or styling changed, check a desktop and a mobile viewport.
- If verification finds a problem, fix it and re-check. Do not open or update the PR with unverified UI.

If browser tools are unavailable (Cloud Agent, headless, app not running), say that. Then rely on TestGuardian’s scoped tests, including a named Chrome Playwright spec when the skill selected E2E. Do not claim the UI was visually verified.
